<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="row" id="problem">
      <p class="lead" style="grid-column:1 / -1">For grant officers, foundations, corporate partnership and CSR leads, co-producers, broadcasters, publishers and philanthropists. If your remit is public engagement with science, cultural participation, STEAM education, or diversity and inclusion, these projects deliver participatory work with measurable engagement and acquittal reporting.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="row" id="what-we-make">
      <h2 class="row-title">What we make</h2>
      <div class="row-body">
        <p>Two ways we build a project. Every project is one of them.</p>
        <h3>Studio</h3>
        <p>We turn science, real and imagined, into music people choose to play. Out of it: an album, a single, a music video, a live show. Research normally waits for people to opt in. A song does not.</p>
        <h3>Field</h3>
        <p>We go where a species lives, and record it there. Out of it: a song, a film, a performance, a schools program. A species in a pop song is a species people carry with them.</p>
        <p>Each project names its own community and its own partner. Young people, multicultural Australia, a school, a university, a gallery. The way we work holds. The people change.</p>
        <p>Most people meet the kangaroo as a postcard, a road sign, a souvenir, a selfie in the park. Kangaroo Time put the behavioural ecology back into that picture, through music, dance and a room of Canberra collaborators. It drew more than 238 features across five continents, and it is still the clearest picture of what the studio does.</p>
        <p>Projects in build stay confidential. The full brief, with the numbers, the team and the timeline, comes on request.</p>
        <p><strong>What you get when you ask.</strong> A one-page brief, a few minutes to read, built to put in front of a panel: the project in one line, what gets made in numbers, who it reaches with the evidence, why now, how it fits your priorities and past grants, the team, the budget with the artist fee named, the ask, what you get back, the timeline, and one contact.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="mailto:hello@wildwoohoo.com?subject=Funding%20conversation">Start a funding conversation</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row" id="partner-retainer">
      <h2 class="row-title">Creative Research Engagement Partner</h2>
      <div class="row-body">
        <p>A 6 to 12 month retainer where the studio is embedded across an organisation's conferences, public engagement, research translation and staff development. One creative translator on the inside, shaping how your ideas meet people all year. Suits universities, research institutes and cultural organisations with a pipeline of moments across the year.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="btn-line" href="mailto:hello@wildwoohoo.com?subject=Creative%20Research%20Engagement%20Partner">Ask about an ongoing partnership</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

